1
00:01:35,439 --> 00:01:39,409
Needless to say, this month is Community Relations Month.

2
00:01:40,177 --> 00:01:43,714
We aim to be a police force loved by the community.

3
00:01:43,914 --> 00:01:48,485
Be sure to treat citizens even more kindly than usual.

4
00:01:48,719 --> 00:01:49,352
Yes, sir!

5
00:01:50,454 --> 00:01:54,157
Excuse me, how can I get to the community center?

6
00:01:54,357 --> 00:01:58,528
It's just around the corner. I'll show you the way.

7
00:01:58,762 --> 00:01:59,896
Let me carry your bag.

8
00:02:00,097 --> 00:02:01,832
Thank you so much.

9
00:02:02,065 --> 00:02:05,435
Chief Ohara, I'll take this old lady to the community center.

10
00:02:05,635 --> 00:02:08,939
Very good. That's how a true police officer should act.

11
00:02:11,541 --> 00:02:13,376
By the way, where's Ryotsu?

12
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:14,444
Well...

13
00:02:15,112 --> 00:02:17,080
He did go out on patrol.

14
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:20,317
But that was around 10 p.m. last night, with Honda-san.

15
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:27,157
Oh dang! The chief's morning briefing will've already started!

16
00:02:27,357 --> 00:02:28,992
He must be furious.

17
00:02:29,192 --> 00:02:31,695
We got carried away and went too far.

18
00:02:31,928 --> 00:02:33,864
It's 'cause you wanted to see Sado Island.

19
00:02:34,097 --> 00:02:37,033
I thought we could be back by dawn

20
00:02:37,234 --> 00:02:37,968
Hmm?

21
00:02:44,174 --> 00:02:45,642
Biker gangs, huh?

22
00:02:45,842 --> 00:02:49,346
We're in a hurry, but they're blocking the way.

23
00:02:49,546 --> 00:02:51,381
Let's blow past them!

24
00:02:51,581 --> 00:02:52,949
Leave it to me.

25
00:02:58,655 --> 00:03:01,191
What's with acting tough on a single patrol bike?

26
00:03:01,391 --> 00:03:03,493
Let's show 'em that "Sigma"

27
00:03:03,693 --> 00:03:06,363
and "Violence Special" control this patch!

28
00:03:06,963 --> 00:03:09,599
We're not letting some cops show off around here!

29
00:03:11,334 --> 00:03:13,370
Hmph, you want to compete with us?

30
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:14,571
Bring it on, punks!

31
00:03:27,384 --> 00:03:29,152
They're no match for us.

32
00:03:29,352 --> 00:03:31,755
You're ten years too early to take us on.

33
00:03:32,155 --> 00:03:34,524
You're too tough! Who the heck are you?

34
00:03:34,925 --> 00:03:37,360
I'm Hayato Honda from the traffic police,

35
00:03:37,561 --> 00:03:38,862
a.k.a. Traffic Cop Honda.

36
00:03:39,229 --> 00:03:42,732
I'm Ryotsu from Kameari Park Police Station.

37
00:03:43,099 --> 00:03:45,702
If you've got a problem, we're always ready to take you on.

38
00:03:48,772 --> 00:03:51,875
Damn, you'll live to regret this, Honda and Ryotsu.

39
00:03:55,011 --> 00:03:59,115
Well, I'm sure the chief will overlook our being late this morning now.

40
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:03,086
After all, we beat up two biker gangs.

41
00:04:03,286 --> 00:04:07,591
It's best to give them a good thrashing, you know.

42
00:04:08,558 --> 00:04:10,894
Oh, it got scratched!

43
00:04:11,094 --> 00:04:13,897
Don't worry. We'll probably get a cash reward.

44
00:04:14,097 --> 00:04:16,633
Really? I'd be happy if that happened.

45
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:20,604
Good morning! We're sorry we're late.

46
00:04:21,438 --> 00:04:24,608
Ryotsu, Honda, what the hell did you guys do?

47
00:04:24,808 --> 00:04:27,110
I just got a call from HQ!

48
00:04:29,579 --> 00:04:32,616
What? We're being suspended from work?

49
00:04:34,417 --> 00:04:36,353
What's going on?

50
00:04:36,586 --> 00:04:38,088
You tell me!

51
00:04:38,288 --> 00:04:42,826
Thanks to you guys, the phones have been flooded with complaints.

52
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:47,430
I apologize deeply. It's my lack of supervision.

53
00:04:47,631 --> 00:04:50,267
Hey, you guys, bow your heads!

54
00:04:50,467 --> 00:04:51,334
Ouch, ouch!

55
00:04:51,534 --> 00:04:53,603
W-Wait a minute!

56
00:04:53,803 --> 00:04:57,607
We beat up two biker gangs!

57
00:04:58,074 --> 00:05:00,310
Why should we be punished?

58
00:05:01,478 --> 00:05:04,180
You got civilian vehicles involved!

59
00:05:04,514 --> 00:05:05,181
What?

60
00:05:05,715 --> 00:05:07,851
The citizens are furious!

61
00:05:08,084 --> 00:05:11,655
Ryotsu, this is the month to strengthen relations with the community.

62
00:05:11,855 --> 00:05:13,790
And look what you've done!

63
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:16,793
You could destroy the trust of the citizens in one go!

64
00:05:17,827 --> 00:05:19,729
I officially hand down your punishment!

65
00:05:20,664 --> 00:05:24,200
For one week from today, both Ryotsu and Honda

66
00:05:24,401 --> 00:05:29,139
will be confined to your homes to reflect fully on your past actions.

67
00:05:29,339 --> 00:05:30,273
Yes, sir.

68
00:05:34,411 --> 00:05:36,379
"NIKONIKO DORMITORY"

69
00:05:36,579 --> 00:05:40,884
Hmph, being suspended at home is basically paid vacation.

70
00:05:41,718 --> 00:05:45,588
Well, I'm gonna build the plastic models that have been piling up.

71
00:05:49,592 --> 00:05:51,895
Hey, you're killing the mood.

72
00:05:52,128 --> 00:05:56,232
We didn't get any money, but we got a week off.

73
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:58,234
You should be happier.

74
00:05:58,435 --> 00:06:02,772
But I can't ride my bike during this time.

75
00:06:03,006 --> 00:06:04,908
What am I supposed to do?

76
00:06:05,875 --> 00:06:07,677
Do whatever you like.

77
00:06:07,877 --> 00:06:09,179
Don't you have any hobbies?

78
00:06:09,546 --> 00:06:12,182
I don't have any hobbies other than motorcycles.

79
00:06:12,582 --> 00:06:17,020
Come to think of it, I don't recall you ever doing anything else.

80
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:17,921
Hmm?

81
00:06:18,722 --> 00:06:20,757
If you have nothing to do, go sleep in your room!

82
00:06:20,991 --> 00:06:23,193
A week will go by in no time!

83
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:48,118
What's that noise?

84
00:06:50,353 --> 00:06:51,254
Hmm?

85
00:06:53,623 --> 00:06:54,724
What was it?

86
00:06:54,924 --> 00:06:56,459
Bike...

87
00:06:58,361 --> 00:07:00,630
H-Honda! Where did you come from?

88
00:07:01,031 --> 00:07:03,033
My bike...

89
00:07:03,233 --> 00:07:06,269
Where's my bike?

90
00:07:07,237 --> 00:07:07,904
Ah!

91
00:07:08,104 --> 00:07:09,139
Bike...

92
00:07:09,506 --> 00:07:12,442
Oh no! My unbuilt plastic model!

93
00:07:13,243 --> 00:07:15,678
Oh, here's my bike.

94
00:07:16,646 --> 00:07:18,214
Huh? No, stop!

95
00:07:18,415 --> 00:07:20,116
I imported that one from America.

96
00:07:20,316 --> 00:07:24,154
It's a Yamaha Virago XV400 Real Type model!

97
00:07:24,421 --> 00:07:25,455
No!

98
00:07:25,655 --> 00:07:27,323
It cost 500 dollars!

99
00:07:27,857 --> 00:07:30,126
Hmm, this is a pretty small bike.

100
00:07:31,461 --> 00:07:34,798
Argh! It's a limited edition that you can't get anymore.

101
00:07:36,766 --> 00:07:39,536
Where's my bike?

102
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:41,438
Hey, wait!

103
00:07:41,638 --> 00:07:45,508
&lt;i&gt;As long as he is around, an enjoyable&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;suspension is just a pipe dream.&lt;/i&gt;

104
00:07:45,708 --> 00:07:47,410
&lt;i&gt;I have to do something.&lt;/i&gt;

105
00:07:50,346 --> 00:07:51,681
Excuse me!

106
00:07:52,082 --> 00:07:54,484
Ryo-chan, are you there?

107
00:07:54,684 --> 00:07:56,419
Yeah, I've been waiting for you.

108
00:07:56,619 --> 00:08:00,356
We brought everything you asked for. But what do you need it for?

109
00:08:00,990 --> 00:08:02,859
To give Honda a hobby!

110
00:08:03,193 --> 00:08:05,361
A hobby other than motorcycles?

111
00:08:05,562 --> 00:08:06,296
Yeah.

112
00:08:06,496 --> 00:08:07,831
Look at him!

113
00:08:08,431 --> 00:08:13,169
Brrrrr.

114
00:08:15,905 --> 00:08:16,840
Honda-san!

115
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,041
Are you okay?

116
00:08:18,274 --> 00:08:19,742
Ouch...

117
00:08:19,976 --> 00:08:21,878
Why am I here?

118
00:08:22,212 --> 00:08:25,815
This is what happens after just one day without his bike.

119
00:08:26,015 --> 00:08:28,284
This is pretty serious.

120
00:08:28,485 --> 00:08:32,722
Right now, Honda's like a salaryman who just retired.

121
00:08:33,289 --> 00:08:37,727
When a man whose life revolves around work retires and loses that sense of purpose,

122
00:08:38,528 --> 00:08:40,563
he suddenly grows old.

123
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:43,533
Especially a guy like the chief, who lives to work.

124
00:08:43,733 --> 00:08:45,668
They're the ones most at risk!

125
00:08:45,869 --> 00:08:47,570
What did you say about me?

126
00:08:50,507 --> 00:08:52,308
Ch-Chief! Why are you here?

127
00:08:53,243 --> 00:08:55,545
I'm responsible for your supervision!

128
00:08:55,745 --> 00:08:58,948
I came to make sure you don't cause any trouble while suspended!

129
00:08:59,182 --> 00:09:01,417
The trouble is already happening.

130
00:09:01,618 --> 00:09:02,318
What?

131
00:09:04,621 --> 00:09:06,322
You idiot!

132
00:09:06,523 --> 00:09:08,558
What are you thinking?

133
00:09:08,758 --> 00:09:11,094
Suspension is a time for reflection.

134
00:09:11,327 --> 00:09:13,963
Using it for hobbies is out of the question!

135
00:09:14,197 --> 00:09:16,733
But Chief, look at this guy.

136
00:09:16,933 --> 00:09:19,369
My bike, where's my bike?

137
00:09:21,804 --> 00:09:24,073
He hasn't eaten properly since yesterday.

138
00:09:24,274 --> 00:09:26,910
If this goes on, he'll get sick!

139
00:09:28,511 --> 00:09:31,514
He might never be able to go back to work again.

140
00:09:31,714 --> 00:09:32,782
N-No way...

141
00:09:33,249 --> 00:09:36,519
Honda is a competent motorcycle police officer.

142
00:09:36,719 --> 00:09:39,522
Of course, you will be held responsible.

143
00:09:39,889 --> 00:09:43,993
You'll be branded as having no management skills and demoted,

144
00:09:44,227 --> 00:09:46,129
then sent to some no-name village.

145
00:09:46,362 --> 00:09:49,465
But rumors spread faster there than in the city,

146
00:09:49,666 --> 00:09:52,135
and soon they'll call you "Ohara the Boss from Hell."

147
00:09:52,669 --> 00:09:57,907
Unable to bear such a life, your wife and daughter will leave home.

148
00:09:58,374 --> 00:10:02,412
With no prospect of promotion or being able to return to Tokyo,

149
00:10:02,612 --> 00:10:07,750
you'll end up spending your old age alone and in despair.

150
00:10:14,958 --> 00:10:17,627
I understand. I'll give you special permission.

151
00:10:17,827 --> 00:10:18,661
Thank you, sir!

152
00:10:18,861 --> 00:10:21,831
That's Chief Ohara, always caring for his subordinates!

153
00:10:22,298 --> 00:10:24,400
He's good at getting people on his side.

154
00:10:24,601 --> 00:10:26,035
That's Ryo-chan's specialty.

155
00:10:26,769 --> 00:10:30,039
The further your hobby is from work, the better.

156
00:10:30,406 --> 00:10:34,143
Coming from a person who puts hobbies before work,

157
00:10:34,344 --> 00:10:35,878
that's very convincing

158
00:10:36,112 --> 00:10:37,247
Shut up!

159
00:10:38,114 --> 00:10:41,184
In Honda's case, it's something as far from motorbikes as possible.

160
00:10:41,884 --> 00:10:43,686
How about collecting coins?

161
00:10:43,886 --> 00:10:45,355
Collecting coins?

162
00:10:45,888 --> 00:10:48,291
You can start today.

163
00:10:48,491 --> 00:10:50,360
Begin with Japanese coins.

164
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:54,597
From one yen to five yen, ten yen, 100 yen, and 500 yen!

165
00:10:54,797 --> 00:10:58,368
A ten yen coin from 1951 is worth more than 100 yen!

166
00:10:58,601 --> 00:11:00,870
I see, coin collecting.

167
00:11:01,070 --> 00:11:03,873
Oh, this one looks like a motorcycle wheel.

168
00:11:04,807 --> 00:11:06,042
It's perfect for you.

169
00:11:06,509 --> 00:11:09,746
A real motorcycle wheel would be better!

170
00:11:11,014 --> 00:11:15,051
Chief! Don't say anything that reminds him of motorbikes!

171
00:11:15,285 --> 00:11:17,020
Sorry, that's right.

172
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:20,323
W-Well, how about knitting?

173
00:11:20,523 --> 00:11:21,924
It'd be perfect for Honda-san.

174
00:11:22,325 --> 00:11:23,393
Knitting?

175
00:11:23,626 --> 00:11:26,629
Yes! I heard it's pretty easy to make a scarf!

176
00:11:26,829 --> 00:11:29,032
A scarf...? Like a muffler?

177
00:11:29,232 --> 00:11:31,067
A muffler!

178
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:32,068
Uh...

179
00:11:32,502 --> 00:11:34,937
D-Dancing is popular nowadays.

180
00:11:35,171 --> 00:11:37,874
Yeah, yeah, dancing. Folk dance.

181
00:11:38,374 --> 00:11:39,876
Folk...

182
00:11:40,710 --> 00:11:41,844
Sounds like fork!

183
00:11:42,245 --> 00:11:44,047
Well... Oh, I know!

184
00:11:44,247 --> 00:11:45,214
Reading!

185
00:11:45,948 --> 00:11:49,752
The story of Baron von Trapp and his family is so moving!

186
00:11:51,087 --> 00:11:54,023
Baron? Baron...

187
00:11:54,223 --> 00:11:56,926
Sounds like "Vroom-vroom"!

188
00:11:57,126 --> 00:11:59,495
Bikes are the best after all!

189
00:12:00,196 --> 00:12:02,732
Quiet, Chief! You're doing this on purpose, aren't you?

190
00:12:02,932 --> 00:12:04,434
S-sorry...

191
00:12:04,901 --> 00:12:08,705
My bike!

192
00:12:23,986 --> 00:12:25,955
It's time, Ryotsu, my man.

193
00:12:26,155 --> 00:12:29,225
Yeah, let's go wild, Honda-san.

194
00:12:45,575 --> 00:12:46,743
Good morning, Ryotsu.

195
00:12:46,943 --> 00:12:48,444
Are you awake, Ryo-chan?

196
00:12:48,644 --> 00:12:51,147
Hey, you're here. Just come on in.

197
00:12:52,281 --> 00:12:53,449
Sorry to disturb you.

198
00:12:53,649 --> 00:12:56,152
Give me a minute. I'm almost done.

199
00:12:56,819 --> 00:12:59,422
Have you been up all night playing video games?

200
00:12:59,622 --> 00:13:03,593
Yeah, because of this guy, I couldn't sleep even if I wanted to.

201
00:13:05,394 --> 00:13:10,967
27,630... 27,631...

202
00:13:11,167 --> 00:13:15,772
27,632... 27,633...

203
00:13:15,972 --> 00:13:20,176
27,634... 27,635...

204
00:13:21,310 --> 00:13:23,780
Honda-san, what are you doing?

205
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:27,784
Hi. If I pop one of these every second,

206
00:13:28,785 --> 00:13:33,289
I only need to pop 431,922 more before I can ride my bike again.

207
00:13:33,589 --> 00:13:37,460
A-Are you gonna keep doing that for your whole suspension?

208
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:39,295
I think he'll get tendonitis.

209
00:13:39,695 --> 00:13:41,430
Yes! I did it!

210
00:13:41,998 --> 00:13:43,966
Come on, Honda. Let's start!

211
00:13:44,634 --> 00:13:46,469
Start what?

212
00:13:47,069 --> 00:13:49,539
You can tell by Nakagawa and Reiko's outfits.

213
00:13:49,772 --> 00:13:51,140
Tennis!

214
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:53,309
Tennis is a classic hobby,

215
00:13:53,509 --> 00:13:55,444
popular with people of all ages and genders.

216
00:13:55,645 --> 00:13:58,714
And Japanese women's tennis is at a high level worldwide!

217
00:13:58,915 --> 00:14:01,617
If you don't play tennis now, you can't say you're Japanese!

218
00:14:02,819 --> 00:14:04,821
Yesterday, we failed in the cultural field.

219
00:14:05,021 --> 00:14:07,023
So I decided to go for sports today.

220
00:14:07,356 --> 00:14:10,092
It's before work, so I can't stay with you for long,

221
00:14:10,326 --> 00:14:11,828
but let's work out a little.

222
00:14:12,028 --> 00:14:14,497
It'll refresh both your body and mind.

223
00:14:14,864 --> 00:14:17,733
Well, I don't want to. I'm doing this.

224
00:14:17,934 --> 00:14:20,636
Doing such a thing will only make you feel depressed!

225
00:14:20,837 --> 00:14:21,704
Now stand up!

226
00:14:21,904 --> 00:14:25,408
No way! Playing tennis will destroy my body!

227
00:14:25,641 --> 00:14:29,045
What kind of biker talks like such a wimp?

228
00:14:29,245 --> 00:14:30,513
Is Ryotsu here?

229
00:14:31,113 --> 00:14:32,114
Ryotsu! Honda!

230
00:14:32,348 --> 00:14:35,518
You two are fired! Fired! I won't show you any more mercy!

231
00:14:35,718 --> 00:14:36,419
What?

232
00:14:36,853 --> 00:14:38,020
Fired?

233
00:14:38,421 --> 00:14:40,523
What happened, Chief?

234
00:14:41,190 --> 00:14:42,725
I'll tell you what!

235
00:14:42,925 --> 00:14:45,394
Even though these guys are on suspension,

236
00:14:45,595 --> 00:14:47,430
they went wild on Loop Road No. 7 last night!

237
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:48,698
What?

238
00:14:49,232 --> 00:14:50,299
Around two a.m.,

239
00:14:50,533 --> 00:14:54,504
two men appeared on Loop Road No. 7, claiming to be "Traffic Cop Honda"

240
00:14:54,704 --> 00:14:56,272
and "Ryotsu of Kameari Park Police"!

241
00:14:57,206 --> 00:15:00,376
They damaged numerous cars under the guise of a crackdown!

242
00:15:00,943 --> 00:15:02,745
Bring out Honda and Ryotsu!

243
00:15:02,945 --> 00:15:04,447
No more arrogant officers!

244
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:09,118
A crowd of protesters has swarmed HQ, causing a huge commotion.

245
00:15:09,752 --> 00:15:11,988
That wasn't us!

246
00:15:12,321 --> 00:15:13,122
Shut up!

247
00:15:13,322 --> 00:15:16,125
So you're saying there're imposters of you guys?

248
00:15:16,325 --> 00:15:20,529
We know from eyewitness testimony that it was definitely you two!

249
00:15:20,863 --> 00:15:21,964
No way!

250
00:15:22,265 --> 00:15:24,767
The official punishment will be announced in a few days.

251
00:15:24,967 --> 00:15:28,971
Honda will probably lose his license and be dismissed from the police!

252
00:15:29,438 --> 00:15:31,974
Dismissed from the police?

253
00:15:32,975 --> 00:15:35,811
No doubt you'll be dismissed too, Ryotsu!

254
00:15:37,613 --> 00:15:40,249
Stay quiet in the dorm until a decision is made!

255
00:15:40,449 --> 00:15:42,985
Got it? Don't go outside in any circumstances!

256
00:15:45,254 --> 00:15:46,822
Putting Ryo-chan aside,

257
00:15:47,256 --> 00:15:51,594
I can't believe Honda-san would ignore his suspension and go on a rampage outside.

258
00:15:53,429 --> 00:15:56,899
Sure, putting Ryotsu aside, in Honda-san's case,

259
00:15:57,099 --> 00:16:01,370
it's more natural to think that an imposter is rampaging around.

260
00:16:01,604 --> 00:16:06,342
So you trust Honda, but not me at all, huh!

261
00:16:06,576 --> 00:16:08,210
N-No, that's not what I meant.

262
00:16:08,444 --> 00:16:09,845
Seeing Honda-san like that...

263
00:16:10,379 --> 00:16:12,348
Huh? He was just here a second ago.

264
00:16:16,352 --> 00:16:17,353
Honda!

265
00:16:18,054 --> 00:16:20,189
N-No way!

266
00:16:24,594 --> 00:16:25,461
Honda!

267
00:16:26,162 --> 00:16:27,697
-Nakagawa! -Okay!

268
00:16:27,930 --> 00:16:28,931
-Reiko! -On it!

269
00:16:29,665 --> 00:16:32,802
Honda-san!

270
00:16:33,002 --> 00:16:34,470
Honda!

271
00:16:41,777 --> 00:16:43,145
Oh, Honda!

272
00:16:45,614 --> 00:16:48,084
You idiot! Stop! What good is dying?

273
00:16:49,151 --> 00:16:50,720
What are you doing?

274
00:16:52,088 --> 00:16:54,156
Honda-san, please calm down.

275
00:16:54,357 --> 00:16:58,227
I'm sure the truth will come out soon and your suspension will be lifted!

276
00:16:58,427 --> 00:17:01,430
That's right. Stay strong, Honda-san!

277
00:17:01,831 --> 00:17:07,003
If you die, your dad, mom, sister Eve, brother Kadoki,

278
00:17:07,203 --> 00:17:10,506
grandpa, and everyone at the traffic police will be sad!

279
00:17:11,207 --> 00:17:14,010
What are you talking about? I was just...

280
00:17:14,210 --> 00:17:16,045
looking at bikes.

281
00:17:16,245 --> 00:17:17,380
What?

282
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:23,085
Don't mislead us like that!

283
00:17:24,253 --> 00:17:24,920
Ryotsu!

284
00:17:25,121 --> 00:17:26,255
Ryo-chan!

285
00:17:31,861 --> 00:17:32,561
Ouch!

286
00:17:32,928 --> 00:17:35,131
Don't move, Ryo-chan.

287
00:17:35,364 --> 00:17:36,265
Jeez.

288
00:17:36,932 --> 00:17:39,368
It was me, so I only got a scratch.

289
00:17:39,568 --> 00:17:42,271
Any normal person would've been seriously injured at best!

290
00:17:42,471 --> 00:17:45,007
If you keep going like this, you really will fall.

291
00:17:45,408 --> 00:17:48,110
That's for sure. There's a good chance of that.

292
00:17:48,444 --> 00:17:50,312
There's no time to lose.

293
00:17:50,546 --> 00:17:52,915
Let's hurry up and catch the real culprits!

294
00:17:53,115 --> 00:17:54,450
I'll help you, too.

295
00:17:54,684 --> 00:17:57,887
Ryo-chan might survive outside the police,

296
00:17:58,087 --> 00:17:59,889
but I feel sorry for Honda-san.

297
00:18:00,089 --> 00:18:02,725
Yeah, putting Ryotsu aside, Honda-san...

298
00:18:02,925 --> 00:18:04,960
Don't bring me up every time!

299
00:18:21,644 --> 00:18:24,146
Looks like there was a big fuss at the police.

300
00:18:24,346 --> 00:18:27,750
If we cause more trouble today, they'll be fired for sure, Toyomi.

301
00:18:27,950 --> 00:18:30,419
Oops, I mean Honda.

302
00:18:30,619 --> 00:18:32,054
Let's go, Ryotsu, my man!

303
00:18:32,254 --> 00:18:32,922
Yeah!

304
00:18:43,799 --> 00:18:44,600
Hey!

305
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:47,470
Get outta the way! Traffic Cop Honda is coming through!

306
00:18:47,670 --> 00:18:50,106
Ryotsu from Kameari Park Police Station is here too!

307
00:18:52,808 --> 00:18:54,176
W-What are you doing?

308
00:18:54,743 --> 00:18:57,012
I hate red cars.

309
00:18:57,213 --> 00:18:59,782
Pay 50,000 yen for violating the color regulations.

310
00:18:59,982 --> 00:19:01,183
N-No way...

311
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:03,919
Shut up! Don't talk back!

312
00:19:04,487 --> 00:19:05,988
I'm Traffic Cop Honda!

313
00:19:06,188 --> 00:19:08,157
With Ryotsu from Kameari Park Police Station!

314
00:19:08,357 --> 00:19:11,227
Anyone with complaints, come out!

315
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:13,496
Yahoo!

316
00:19:15,865 --> 00:19:16,765
What?

317
00:19:22,471 --> 00:19:23,339
Huh?

318
00:19:26,408 --> 00:19:27,409
Don't let them get away!

319
00:19:27,643 --> 00:19:28,944
Ryotsu! We're descending!

320
00:19:29,145 --> 00:19:29,845
Okay!

321
00:19:33,949 --> 00:19:35,151
Let's go, Honda!

322
00:19:35,351 --> 00:19:36,018
But...

323
00:19:36,552 --> 00:19:39,822
H-How do we get down from so high up?

324
00:19:40,022 --> 00:19:41,223
Come on!

325
00:19:41,423 --> 00:19:43,859
Stop complaining and just get on!

326
00:19:46,595 --> 00:19:48,998
Prepare yourselves, imposters!

327
00:20:00,209 --> 00:20:01,911
-Let's go, Ryotsu! -Yeah!

328
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:12,822
W-What?

329
00:20:18,561 --> 00:20:20,563
How dare you use our names!

330
00:20:20,763 --> 00:20:22,565
You'll pay for this!

331
00:20:22,765 --> 00:20:23,766
Jeez, the real ones!

332
00:20:23,999 --> 00:20:25,000
We can't get caught!

333
00:20:29,939 --> 00:20:31,106
Don't let them escape!

334
00:20:31,307 --> 00:20:32,274
No chance!

335
00:20:35,945 --> 00:20:38,080
"SUBWAY STATION"

336
00:20:46,789 --> 00:20:48,557
Stop right there!

337
00:21:15,751 --> 00:21:16,418
What?

338
00:21:19,088 --> 00:21:21,156
Argh! Get out of the way!

339
00:21:22,157 --> 00:21:23,993
Don't come this way!

340
00:21:34,970 --> 00:21:37,539
That'll be 736 yen.

341
00:21:37,773 --> 00:21:38,941
Welcome.

342
00:21:39,508 --> 00:21:41,243
Hold it!

343
00:21:49,852 --> 00:21:51,854
You jerks! Show us who you are!

344
00:22:00,729 --> 00:22:01,664
Damn it!

345
00:22:03,999 --> 00:22:06,035
Oh no!

346
00:22:07,303 --> 00:22:08,737
Oh, it's those punks!

347
00:22:09,471 --> 00:22:11,707
The head of the bike gang "Violence Special"!

348
00:22:12,141 --> 00:22:14,276
And the other one is the leader of "Sigma"!

349
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:16,178
We're busted!

350
00:22:16,378 --> 00:22:17,513
I get it.

351
00:22:17,713 --> 00:22:21,483
You were doing this out of revenge for being crushed by the two of us.

352
00:22:22,017 --> 00:22:22,718
Let's lose 'em!

353
00:22:25,387 --> 00:22:26,689
We won't let you get away!

354
00:22:26,889 --> 00:22:29,024
"KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION"

355
00:22:29,224 --> 00:22:32,995
Damn, if I get fired because of Ryotsu, I'll make him pay for it.

356
00:22:35,331 --> 00:22:38,133
Come on! How long are they gonna chase us?

357
00:22:44,206 --> 00:22:47,977
You guys did one thing you shouldn't have done!

358
00:22:48,711 --> 00:22:50,245
You pissed me off!

359
00:22:52,581 --> 00:22:54,750
Go to hell, scumbags!

360
00:23:18,207 --> 00:23:19,174
We did it!

361
00:23:19,375 --> 00:23:21,443
This will prove our innocence.

362
00:23:21,643 --> 00:23:24,413
Now I'll be able to ride my bike with pride again.

363
00:23:39,495 --> 00:23:40,829
Ch-Chief!

364
00:23:41,397 --> 00:23:43,098
Ryotsu! Honda!

365
00:23:43,298 --> 00:23:45,367
It was you two after all!

366
00:23:45,968 --> 00:23:48,137
No, there's a good reason for this...

367
00:23:49,438 --> 00:23:50,939
I've had enough!

368
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:53,275
You're fired! Absolutely fired!

369
00:23:53,842 --> 00:23:58,313
I said you're fired, and I mean it!

370
00:24:03,051 --> 00:24:08,891
LET'S BOOST THE RATINGS!
